Hi <%= @notice.name %> admins,

Effective immediately, Firezone checks that Microsoft Entra sign-ins come from
a tenant verified on the authentication provider being used. Users from an
unlisted tenant cannot sign in until that tenant is verified.

We found stored Entra identities in your Firezone account <%= @notice.slug %>
from tenants that are not currently verified on an enabled Entra provider.
To support continued authentication, review the tenant IDs below and verify
each tenant whose users should keep access.

ADDITIONAL TENANTS TO VERIFY

Verify these tenants on your existing provider. The domain labels come from
email addresses on stored identities, not verified tenant names.
<%= for tenant <- @notice.tenants do %>
<%= Enum.join(tenant.domains, ", ") %>
Tenant ID: <%= tenant.id %>
<% end %>
Each tenant can belong to only one Entra provider in your Firezone account.
If a listed tenant is already verified on a disabled provider, re-enable that
provider instead.

WHAT TO DO

1. Open Settings -> Authentication in your Firezone account:
   <%= @settings_url %>

2. Edit your existing Entra provider. Under Verified tenants, click
   Verify another tenant.

3. Sign in with an account from the additional tenant that has the Global
   Administrator or Privileged Role Administrator role, and complete
   verification. Check that the new row shows the intended tenant ID above.

4. Repeat for each additional tenant that needs access, then click Save.
   Users from all verified tenants can continue using the same sign-in option.

See the Entra authentication guide for details:
https://www.firezone.dev/kb/authenticate/entra

If you need help, contact support@firezone.dev or reach out in your support
channel.
